# Keep the oracle-frozen artifacts byte-exact (audit re-review P1-4): never apply
# end-of-line or other text normalization, so their SHA-256 pins in
# external_models/mccalip_thoughts/PINS.json stay valid across platforms/checkouts.
external_models/mccalip_thoughts/math.js               -text
external_models/mccalip_thoughts/generate_oracle.js    -text
external_models/mccalip_thoughts/expected_outputs.json -text

# Same reasoning for the Biswas/Suncatcher vendored script: its SHA-256 pin in
# external_models/biswas_suncatcher/PINS.json is enforced byte-for-byte by
# tests/test_biswas_suncatcher_reference.py::test_vendored_script_byte_identical.
# The pinned upstream file is LF; force an LF checkout on every platform so git
# autocrlf cannot rewrite LF->CRLF on Windows and break the hash. `text eol=lf`
# also normalizes CRLF->LF on commit, so the blob self-heals (R2 Track-R
# byte-identity guard must be platform-robust).
external_models/biswas_suncatcher/report_one_thermal.py text eol=lf
